direct-marked-args
owner: fable-5.1 session 53f400ad
started: 2026-09-16
what: `!f(!f(5))` — a mark inside the ARGUMENT of a marked call — was
  refused as "a mark under a lambda", and the lambda was the macro's
  own: the defer-every-call rule wraps the call in `Free.delay(() =>
  …)` before compilation, so the argument's mark lands under that
  thunk. A call whose arguments carry marks must not be deferred: the
  arguments bind first, and the call is built in the continuation.
  Found while writing `Delim.shift(p)(k => direct { !k(!k(5)) })`,
  which is the natural spelling of a continuation invoked twice.
files: src/main/scala/Direct.scala, src/test/scala/TestDirectDeep.scala,
  specs/direct-macro.md, CHANGELOG.md
